        "Attributes": [
          {
            "Id": 758491,
            "attributeType": "LongString",
            "attributeName": "AIDescription",
            "attributeRelationType": "None",
            "Value": "The PlayStation (originally codenamed PSX) is a home video game console developed and marketed by Sony Computer Entertainment, released in Japan in 1994 and globally throughout 1995. It marked Sony's entry into the console market, challenging Nintendo and Sega. Designed with an emphasis on 3D polygon graphics and streamlined game development, the PlayStation fostered a vast and diverse game library, attracting numerous third-party developers. \n\nCritically acclaimed titles like *Final Fantasy VII*, *Crash Bandicoot*, *Spyro the Dragon*, *Metal Gear Solid*, *Tomb Raider*, and *Gran Turismo* became instant classics, with *Gran Turismo* becoming the console's best-selling game. The PlayStation revolutionized the industry by embracing CD-ROMs and appealing to a broader, more adult audience. Ultimately, it sold over 100 million units, paving the way for the PlayStation 2 and establishing Sony as a dominant force in gaming."
          },
